# Repository Context Loading

Context loading is **not optional** — first step before any work.

## Before ANY Changes

1. `CONTEXT.md`
2. `AGENTS.md`
3. Mandatory docs: GOVERNANCE, ARCHITECTURE, TESTING, COMMENTS, SECURITY, DEPENDENCIES, RELEASES, CI_CD

## MUST / MUST NOT

- Read CONTEXT first, AGENTS second, mandatory docs (no “unrelated” skip)
- Must not skip / selectively read / begin before load complete

## Precedence

CONTEXT > GOVERNANCE > ARCHITECTURE > domain docs > inline comments

## Non-negotiables (summary)

- Lambda Node 24 (`nodejs24.x`) aligned with CI; TypeScript strict; ≥80% Jest statements; Conventional Commits + Husky
- No hardcoded secrets; no secrets in zips/logs
- No Express/Fastify; preserve per-route packages and webpack packaging
- Prefer latest deps/Actions/runtimes unless peers truly block (see `docs/DEPENDENCIES.md`)
- Quality gate: `make preflight`
